Authelia on FenrirOS
====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no configuration, no
secret and no user database.

1. Write /etc/authelia/configuration.yml from
   /usr/share/doc/authelia/config.template.yml (root:authelia, mode 0640).
   Generate your own secrets (`authelia crypto rand --length 64 --charset
   alphanumeric`) for the session, storage encryption key and identity
   validation JWT; point storage at /var/lib/authelia (SQLite) or a database
   server; choose a notifier (SMTP, or the filesystem notifier for testing).
2. Create a users file (file authentication backend) with
   `authelia crypto hash generate argon2` for the password hashes, or use an
   LDAP backend.
3. dinitctl enable authelia

Authelia listens on the address given in the configuration (the sample uses
tcp://:9091); it is meant to sit behind a reverse proxy (forward auth). The
web portal in this package is built from source.
